{"name":"Ocean Dream","hex":"#d4dde2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ocean","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of the large bodies of water separating the continents.","The continuous body of salt water covering a majority of the Earth's surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ocean"},{"term":"dream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Imaginary events seen in the mind while sleeping.","A hope or wish."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To see imaginary events in one's mind while sleeping.","To hope, to wish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spirit of London (ship)","blocks":[{"text":"Spirit of London was an Italian built cruise ship that entered service with P&O in 1972. Afer being operated by a number of owners and being renamed New Flamenco, in January 2012 is was renamed Ocean Dream. After serving as a hotel ship it sank off Thailand in 2016 and was scrapped."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/8a/Launching_1972.jpg/330px-Launching_1972.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spirit_of_London_(ship)"},{"title":"MS Tropicale","blocks":[{"text":"MS Tropicale was a cruise ship that entered service in 1982, and was one of the pioneering cruise ships in the modernization of the cruise industry. She was Carnival Cruises Line's first newly built ship, initially operating mainly in the Mexican Riviera and the Caribbean."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/MS_Tropicale_1996_im_Hafen_von_Martinique_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-MS_Tropicale_1996_im_Hafen_von_Martinique_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MS_Tropicale"},{"title":"Ocean","blocks":[{"text":"The ocean is the body of salt water that covers approximately 70.8% of Earth. The ocean is conventionally divided into large bodies of water, which are also referred to as oceans, and are themselves mostly divided into seas, gulfs, and subsequent bodies of water. The ocean contains 97% of Earth's water and is the primary component of Earth's hydrosphere, acting as a huge reservoir of heat for Earth's energy budget, as well as for its carbon cycle and water cycle, forming the basis for climate and weather patterns worldwide. The ocean is essential to life on Earth, harboring most of Earth's animals and protist life. It originated photosynthesis and therefore Earth's atmospheric oxygen, and still supplies half of it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Pacific_Ocean_as_viewed_from_GOES-18_on_September_23%2C_2023.jpg/330px-Pacific_Ocean_as_viewed_from_GOES-18_on_September_23%2C_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ocean"},{"title":"Dream","blocks":[{"text":"A dream is a succession of images, dynamic scenes and situations, ideas, emotions, and sensations that usually occur involuntarily in the mind during certain stages of sleep. Humans generally spend more than two hours dreaming per night, and each dream lasts around 5–20 minutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg/330px-A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dream"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/%22Southern_Cross%22_-_Copenhagen%2C_1995.jpg/500px-%22Southern_Cross%22_-_Copenhagen%2C_1995.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/%22Southern_Cross%22_-_Copenhagen%2C_1995.jpg/1280px-%22Southern_Cross%22_-_Copenhagen%2C_1995.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumb